WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.211
Business continuity in operational technology is the ability to maintain or restore critical physical operations at an acceptable level after disruption.

00:00:10.211 --> 00:00:22.691
The mission may be safe production, electricity delivery, water treatment, transportation, environmental control, or another service that depends on people, equipment, and control systems working together.

00:00:22.691 --> 00:00:27.910
Continuity does not always mean keeping every system fully available.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:38.575
A site may shift to a safe degraded mode, reduce capacity, isolate a process, use alternate equipment, or perform a controlled shutdown.

00:00:38.575 --> 00:00:45.155
Plans define the minimum acceptable operation and the conditions for returning to normal.

00:00:45.155 --> 00:00:51.282
IT service continuity often focuses on restoring applications, data, and user access.

00:00:51.282 --> 00:01:04.216
OT continuity includes those concerns but also considers process state, equipment sequencing, utility dependencies, operator visibility, product quality, environmental consequence, and the safety of shutdown and restart.

00:01:04.216 --> 00:01:10.796
Disaster recovery and incident response support continuity but are not identical to it.

00:01:10.796 --> 00:01:13.746
Recovery restores technology and data.

00:01:13.746 --> 00:01:17.604
Incident response contains and investigates an event.

00:01:17.604 --> 00:01:24.638
Continuity coordinates the broader operational choices that protect the mission while those activities occur.

00:01:24.638 --> 00:01:27.588
Safety comes before production pressure.

00:01:27.588 --> 00:01:37.799
A fast technical recovery is not successful if process conditions, logic integrity, alarms, interlocks, or field equipment have not been validated.

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:43.471
Operations and engineering need authority to decide when restoration is safe.

00:01:43.471 --> 00:01:53.682
A useful continuity plan connects critical processes to assets, people, vendors, spares, utilities, communications, backups, fallback procedures, and tested recovery sequences.

00:01:53.682 --> 00:02:01.171
It prepares the organization to make deliberate decisions when normal automation and information are unavailable.
